9. MODULE 7 - MAINTENANCE RECORDS MODULE
================================================================================

Purpose:
  Allows admins to schedule and track vehicle maintenance activities.
  Helps keep the fleet in optimal condition.

Model:
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
  | File                                        | Description                      |
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
  | MaintenanceRecord.php                       | Maintenance record entity        |
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+

Controller:
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
  | File                                        | Description                      |
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
  | Admin/MaintenanceController.php             | Admin maintenance management     |
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+

View:
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
  | File                                        | Description                      |
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+
  | admin/maintenance/index.blade.php           | Maintenance records listing      |
  +---------------------------------------------+----------------------------------+

Database Table - maintenance_records:
  +-------------------------+-------------------+-------------------------------+
  | Column                  | Type              | Description                   |
  +-------------------------+-------------------+-------------------------------+
  | id                      | BIGINT (PK)       | Auto-increment primary key    |
  | car_id                  | BIGINT (FK)       | References cars.id            |
  | title                   | VARCHAR           | Maintenance title             |
  | description             | TEXT              | Detailed description          |
  | scheduled_date          | DATE              | Scheduled maintenance date    |
  | completed_date          | DATE              | Actual completion date        |
  | cost                    | DECIMAL(10,2)     | Maintenance cost (default: 0) |
  | status                  | ENUM              | Scheduled/In Progress/        |
  |                         |                   | Completed/Cancelled           |
  | created_at              | TIMESTAMP         | Record creation time          |
  | updated_at              | TIMESTAMP         | Last update time              |
  +-------------------------+-------------------+-------------------------------+

Routes (Admin):
  GET  /admin/maintenance              -> View all maintenance records
  POST /admin/maintenance              -> Create new maintenance record
  POST /admin/maintenance/{id}/complete -> Mark maintenance as completed

Maintenance Status Flow:
  Scheduled -> In Progress -> Completed
         \-> Cancelled

Key Methods in MaintenanceRecord Model:
  - getFormattedCostAttribute()  : Returns "₹X,XXX.XX" format
  - getStatusBadgeAttribute()    : Returns CSS class for status badge


